# HTTP proxy (China)

Many sites are unreachable without a local proxy (Google, Twitter/X, YouTube,
npm registry mirrors that fail, VS Marketplace, Open VSX, AI APIs, etc.).

- Default proxy: **`http://localhost:8118`**
- Prefer env when calling tools that honor it:

```bash
export http_proxy=http://localhost:8118
export https_proxy=http://localhost:8118
export HTTP_PROXY=http://localhost:8118
export HTTPS_PROXY=http://localhost:8118
```

- For CLIs that take an explicit proxy flag, pass
  **`http-proxy http://localhost:8118`** (or the tool’s equivalent).
  Do **not** use this to run external machine-translation tools — see
  **translations.mdc** (agent hand-translates; no `trans` / Google / etc.).
- Do not assume raw access to blocked hosts will work; set the proxy first.
